    "title": "KPop Demon Hunters adult Happy Meal is coming — with umami fries and purple ‘Demon Sauce’",
    "text": "Valerie Williams, SavorNation Updated: Mar 25, 2026 / 03:56 PM CDT McDonald’s (SavorNation) – Unless you live under a rock (or don’t have kids), you know all about KPop Demon Hunters. The Netflix animated movie about a KPop girl group that performs by day and slays demons by night was the hit of the summer. Now, KPop icons HUNTR/X and the Saja Boys, the bands from the film, are the stars of two adult Happy Meals set to hit McDonald’s locations on March 31. If you’re not familiar with the film’s plot, here’s a quick drill-down: The girl group, HUNTR/X, has Rumi, Mira, Zoey, pop idols who just happen to be demon hunters. The Saja Boys, demons disguised as a boy band, are their rivals. The movie’s featured song “Golden” won multiple awards including an Oscar. Now, McDonald’s is hopping on the KPop fandom wagon with a set of Happy Meals dedicated to celebrating the film. The boys are the stars of the breakfast version of the KPop Happy Meals. It features a Spicy Saja McMuffin (a Sausage McMuffin with Egg, topped with a peppery Spicy Saja Sauce), hash browns and a small soft drink. The HUNTR/X meal includes a 10-piece Chicken McNuggets, medium soft drink and limited edition menu items including Ramyeon McShaker Fries, a spicy umami version of McDonald’s fries, and two new sauces: Hunter Sauce, a sweet chili, and Demon Sauce, a bold mustard The new Derpy McFlurry is inspired by Derpy Tiger, a lovable pet tiger who becomes Rumi’s loyal sidekick. The treat features vanilla soft serve with berry popping pearls blended with a wild berry sauce. What’s a Happy Meal without a toy? This time, it’s fully KPop core with an exclusive photocard for either HUNTR/X or the Saja Boys. A Derpy access card is included with each meal featuring a QR code that can be scanned to reveal a unique code to enter on the McDonald’s app by April 26 to unlock exclusive content and find out which KPop group wins the Battle for the Fans. SavorNation is reader-supported and may earn an affiliate commission.",
